# Web operator console — frontend env vars.
#
# Vite injects every `VITE_*` value at build time, so these are PUBLIC
# (anything that needs to stay secret belongs on the FastAPI server).
#
# The frontend ships with sensible Replit defaults — every value below
# is optional; leaving the file empty (or removing it) reproduces the
# Replit-hosted behavior the app has always had.

# --- Auth (Clerk) ---
# Required in production. The Replit Auth pane provisions this for you;
# set it manually for non-Replit deployments.
# VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...
# VITE_CLERK_PROXY_URL=https://clerk.example.com

# --- Backend host knob (Mac Studio cutover) ---
# When EMPTY (default), every API call and WebSocket connects back to
# the same origin the frontend was served from — i.e. the standard
# Replit deployment where the FastAPI server lives behind the same
# proxy.
#
# When SET to an absolute URL, the SAME bundled frontend is pointed at
# a self-hosted backend (e.g. a Mac Studio behind a Cloudflare tunnel).
# REST goes to `${VITE_API_URL}<path>`; WebSockets auto-upgrade
# http→ws / https→wss against the same origin. See
# `MIGRATION_MAC_STUDIO.md` at the repo root for the full cutover flow.
#
# Examples:
#   VITE_API_URL=https://api.yourdomain.com
#   VITE_API_URL=http://mac-studio.local:8000
#
# VITE_API_URL=

# --- Stripe (publishable key only — secret stays on the server) ---
# VITE_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...
